\vspace{0.22cm}
{\Large\bfseries\color{ChapterStone} 全書一句話 \textperiodcentered\ The Whole Book in Three Sentences}

\vspace{0.30cm}
\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{ScriptureBg}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\centering\vspace{0.2cm}
\normalsize\color{CommentaryBrown}
良人\textbf{\color{HandClay!80!black}屬我}，我也\textbf{\color{HandClay!80!black}屬他}。\hfill{\scriptsize\color{ChapterStone} 2:16}\\[0.4em]
我\textbf{\color{HandClay!80!black}屬我的良人}，我的良人也\textbf{\color{HandClay!80!black}屬我}。\hfill{\scriptsize\color{ChapterStone} 6:3}\\[0.4em]
我\textbf{\color{HandClay!80!black}屬我的良人}，他也\textbf{\color{ChapterStone}戀慕我}。\hfill{\scriptsize\color{ChapterStone} 7:10}\\[0.6em]
\footnotesize\itshape
“My beloved is mine, and I am his.” \quad “I am my beloved's and my beloved is mine.” \quad
“I am my beloved's, and his desire is for me.”\\[0.4em]
\small\color{ChapterStone} 雅歌 2:16；6:3；7:10 \textperiodcentered\ Song of Songs 2:16; 6:3; 7:10
\vspace{0.2cm}
\end{minipage}}

\vspace{0.35cm}
{\small\color{TextGray} 八章經文 \textperiodcentered\ 十五篇研讀 \textperiodcentered\ 四卷 \textperiodcentered\ 愛先被呼喚，園子從裏面打開，印記蓋上，仍然盼望\\
\textit{Eight chapters of the Song in fifteen studies \textperiodcentered\ four volumes \textperiodcentered\ love is called, the garden opens from within, the seal is set, and the longing stays}}

\vspace{0.30cm}
{\small
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.3}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.8cm}p{2.4cm}p{6.9cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{卷} & \textbf{研讀篇} & \textbf{在全書的展開} \\
\midrule
卷一：渴慕與尋見 & 1-6篇 & 一個「願」字；他來了；夜間尋見；婚禮的行列；兩次「不要叫醒」 \\
卷二：園子的敞開 & 7-8篇 & 關鎖的園；「願我的良人進入自己園裏」；「我進了我的園」 \\
卷三：失落與重尋 & 9-11篇 & 敲門、遲疑、他轉身走了；她說出他是誰；他仍稱她獨一 \\
卷四：渴想的反轉與印記 & 12-15篇 & 王被髮綹繫住；「他也戀慕我」；愛如死之堅強；求你快來 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{ScriptureGold}{\rule{2.5in}{0.7pt}}
\vspace{0.3cm}

{\bfseries\color{ChapterStone} 讀經之鑰 \textperiodcentered\ How to Read This Book}

\vspace{0.18cm}
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\small\color{TextGray}
這是一首情詩，本書先把它當作情詩來讀：一對男女的愛，是神所造的好。\\
同時，聖經自己說婚姻是基督與教會的奧祕（弗 5:32）；\\
本書把「字面」「直接的類比」「歷代的寓意讀法」分開寫，不讓其中一種取消另一種。\\[0.5em]
\textit{\footnotesize
This is a love poem, and this book reads it first as a love poem: the love of a man and
a woman is God's good gift. Scripture itself calls marriage a mystery concerning Christ and
the church (Eph 5:32); this book keeps the literal reading, the direct analogy and the
church's allegorical tradition apart, and lets none cancel the others.}
\end{minipage}

\vfill
{\scriptsize\color{LightGray} PubHub 三書精讀系統 \textperiodcentered\ Soli Deo Gloria}

